{
  "_README": [
    "THE DETERMINISM PIN FOR Hash64 AND DeterministicRng (14 section 8.0 / 8.1).",
    "",
    "*** CHANGING A ROW IN THIS FILE IS A DETERMINISM BREAK, NEVER A TEST FIX. ***",
    "",
    "Every row is a committed (inputs -> hash) fact. If a row starts failing, the",
    "implementation changed, not the expectation: every seed derivation, every board",
    "layout, every die roll and every drop the game has ever produced for a given seed",
    "just moved. Saved runs stop reproducing, client and server stop agreeing on a",
    "battle, and bug-report replays become fiction. Fix the code.",
    "",
    "The only legitimate edit is ADDING rows. If a row must genuinely change, that is a",
    "deliberate, announced break: it needs its own commit, a note in the decision log,",
    "and a migration story for every persisted runSeed and stream counter.",
    "",
    "These rows are asserted byte-identical on every LIVE target platform -- Linux x64",
    "(server) and Android ARM64 -- by the cross-platform determinism job (14 section",
    "8.2). The iOS ARM64 leg is authored and gated off with iOS itself (16 D34) and is",
    "the first thing to re-enable if iOS returns. They are embedded in the",
    "SlayIdleRepeat.Core.Tests assembly so that job finds them regardless of working",
    "directory.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE. These rows were NOT generated from SlayIdleRepeat.Core. They were",
    "generated from Microsoft's System.IO.Hashing.XxHash64 -- a second, independent",
    "XXH64 implementation -- driven by a canonical encoder transcribed directly from",
    "the 14 section 8.0 spec table. That generator first reproduced all nine published",
    "xxHash sanity vectors below, which is what proves it is really XXH64 and not just",
    "self-consistent. SlayIdleRepeat.Core then had to match it."
  ],

  "xxh64PublishedKnownAnswerVectors": {
    "_README": [
      "The reference implementation's own known-answer tests, copied verbatim from",
      "cli/xsum_sanity_check.c in https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash (XSUM_XXH64_testdata).",
      "This is the external check: an implementation that passes these IS XXH64.",
      "",
      "The input is the first `length` bytes of the sanity buffer, which xsum builds as:",
      "",
      "    byteGen = PRIME32;",
      "    for (i = 0; i < len; i++) { buffer[i] = (U8)(byteGen >> 56); byteGen *= PRIME64; }",
      "",
      "with PRIME32 = 2654435761 and PRIME64 = 11400714785074694797. Note that xsum's",
      "PRIME64 is NOT XXH_PRIME64_1 (11400714785074694791) -- the last digit differs.",
      "",
      "`seed` is the XXH64 hash-seed parameter. SlayIdleRepeat's Hash64 always uses 0;",
      "the PRIME32-seeded rows are here because they exercise the seed initialisation of",
      "the accumulators, which the seed-0 rows cannot."
    ],
    "bufferGenerator": {
      "prime32": "2654435761",
      "prime64": "11400714785074694797",
      "byteExpression": "buffer[i] = (byte)(byteGen >> 56), then byteGen *= prime64"
    },
    "rows": [
    { "length": 0, "seed": "0x0000000000000000", "hash": "0xef46db3751d8e999" },
    { "length": 0, "seed": "0x000000009e3779b1", "hash": "0xac75fda2929b17ef" },
    { "length": 1, "seed": "0x0000000000000000", "hash": "0xe934a84adb052768" },
