  "deterministicRngVectors": {
    "_README": [
      "DeterministicRng over the same Hash64. Draw i of stream s over seed r is",
      "Hash64(r, s, i); the accessors are pure functions of that one draw:",
      "",
      "  nextUInt   = (uint)(draw >> 32)                      -- the top 32 bits",
      "  nextDouble = (draw >> 11) * 2^-53                    -- the 53-bit construction",
      "  range      = min + (int)(draw % (ulong)(max - min))  -- modulo bias accepted",
      "",
      "`nextDoubleBits` is the IEEE-754 bit pattern of nextDouble, asserted exactly -- no",
      "tolerance. The construction is exact in binary floating point (a 53-bit integer",
      "times a power of two), so any tolerance would only hide a real divergence. The",
      "decimal `nextDouble` alongside it is round-trippable and for human eyes only.",
      "",
      "nextDouble is NOT rounded to 4 decimal places. The 4-dp rule of 14 section 8.2",
      "applies to combat ACCUMULATION points, not to a raw draw; rounding here would",
      "throw away 49 bits of every draw the game makes."
    ],
    "rows": [
    {
